.TH SECSTORE2 2
.SH NAME
secstore2 \- Monocypher-backed secure store file format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "secstore2.m";
secstore2 := load Secstore2 Secstore2->PATH;

Head: adt {
	t, m, p, keylen:	int;
	salt:			array of byte;
	nonce:			array of byte;
	ptxlen, epoch, rev:	int;
	ownerlen, namelen:	int;
	owner, name:		string;
};

init:		fn();
headinit:	fn(owner, name: string): ref Head;
clone:		fn(h: ref Head): ref Head;
parsehead:	fn(in: array of byte): (int, ref Head, string);
derive:		fn(h: ref Head, pass: array of byte): (array of byte, string);
sealkey:	fn(h: ref Head, key: array of byte, plain: array of byte):
			(array of byte, string);
seal:		fn(h: ref Head, pass: array of byte, plain: array of byte):
			(array of byte, string);
openkey:	fn(in: array of byte, h: ref Head, key: array of byte):
			(array of byte, string);
open:		fn(in: array of byte, pass: array of byte):
			(array of byte, ref Head, string);
digest:		fn(in: array of byte): array of byte;
samekdf:	fn(a, b: ref Head): int;
validname:	fn(name: string): int;
hex:		fn(a: array of byte): string;
unhex:		fn(s: string): array of byte;
wipe:		fn(a: array of byte);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Secstore2
implements the
.I secstore2
file format: one encrypted file is one blob, sealed with Argon2id,
XChaCha20-Poly1305 and BLAKE2b-256.
The layout is:
.EX
offset	size	field
0	4	magic "SC2\\0"
4	1	version = 2
5	1	kdf = 1 (Argon2id)
6	1	aead = 1 (XChaCha20-Poly1305)
7	1	flags = 0
8	4	t (passes, LE32)
12	4	m (KiB, LE32)
16	4	p (lanes, LE32)
20	4	keylen = 32
24	16	salt
40	24	nonce
64	4	plaintext length
68	4	epoch
72	4	revision
76	4	owner length
80	4	name length
84	12	reserved (zero)
96	...	owner bytes, name bytes
...	...	ciphertext
...	16	Poly1305 tag
last	32	BLAKE2b-256 over everything before it
.EE
.PP
The 96-byte header and the owner and name bytes are the associated data
passed to the AEAD, so a renamed, re-versioned or parameter-downgraded
file fails authentication even if the trailing digest is recomputed.
The digest is a content identifier for synchronisation, not a password
check.
.PP
The file key is
.IP
.EX
master  = Argon2id(password, salt, t, m KiB, p, 32)
filekey = BLAKE2b-256("secstore2 file" || master)
.EE
.IP
The client enforces a floor of 64 MiB and a ceiling of 256 MiB for
.IR m ,
and this implementation requires
.IR p =1
because the
.I Mono
Argon2id binding is single-lane.
The default parameters are
.IR t =3,
.IR m =262144
and
.IR p =1.
.PP
.B Init
must be called before the functions that use
.IR Mono ;
it loads the module and is idempotent.
.PP
.B Headinit
returns a header with the default KDF parameters, zero salt and nonce,
epoch and revision one, and the given owner and name.
The caller fills in salt, nonce, epoch and revision as needed.
.B Clone
returns a copy of a header.
.PP
.B Parsehead
checks the magic, version, algorithms, lengths and total size.
It returns
.RI ( ok , " h" , " err" );
.I ok
is one on success, and
.I err
is a diagnostic otherwise.
.PP
.B Derive
returns the file key for a header and password, enforcing the KDF
floor, ceiling and parameter limits before doing any work.
.B Sealkey
and
.B Openkey
seal and open a blob with an already derived key;
.B Seal
and
.B Open
combine the key derivation with them.
.B Open
returns
.RI ( plain , " h" , " err" ).
.PP
.B Digest
returns the BLAKE2b-256 digest of the whole blob.
.B Samekdf
reports whether two headers derive the same key from the same password.
.PP
.B Validname
accepts
.BR A-Za-z0-9._-
with no leading dot and at most 255 bytes.
.B Hex
and
.B Unhex
convert between bytes and lower-case hexadecimal.
.B Wipe
zeroes a buffer; call it on every key, password and plaintext array.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/secstore2.b
.br
.B /module/secstore2.m
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR secstore2 (1),
.IR secstore (1),
.IR mono (2)
.SH BUGS
Only one Argon2id lane is supported.
